@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8000
# Paste your active token from /auth/login here:
@token = replace_with_actual_token

### 1. Create a Supplier
POST {{baseUrl}}/suppliers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Lagos Pharma Distributors",
  "phone": "+2348000000000",
  "email": "contact@lagospharma.com"
}

### 2. Create a Batch (Make sure product_id 1 exists)
POST {{baseUrl}}/batches
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "product_id": 1,
  "supplier_id": 1,
  "batch_number": "BATCH-2026-A1",
  "quantity_received": 100,
  "expiry_date": "2027-10-20",
  "received_date": "2026-10-20"
}

### 3. Test Expiring Soon Query
GET {{baseUrl}}/batches/expiring-soon?days=365
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Adjust Stock (Sell 5 items)
POST {{baseUrl}}/batches/1/adjustments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity_change": -5,
  "reason": "sold",
  "note": "Morning sale"
}

### 5. Attempt Invalid Adjustment (Would go negative)
POST {{baseUrl}}/batches/1/adjustments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity_change": -5000,
  "reason": "damaged",
  "note": "Water damage"
}

### 6. View Adjustment History for Batch
GET {{baseUrl}}/batches/1/adjustments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}